@startuml uc-05-job-lifecycle
' Copyright 2026 Muhammad Salah
' SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
title Job lifecycle across use cases (UC-O1 … UC-O6)

[*] --> Queued : Operator starts\ncapture / restore / copy
Queued --> Probing : UC-C6
Probing --> Failed : blocking check fails\n(never starts work)
Probing --> Cloning : docker / k8s
Probing --> Running : local / ssh
Cloning --> Running : clone hung & ready
Cloning --> Failed : cannot create clone

Running --> Verifying : work streamed\nand sealed
Running --> Backoff : retryable error\n(timeout, reset, 5xx, throttle)
Running --> Interrupted : connection dropped
Running --> Cancelling : Operator cancels (UC-O3)

Backoff --> Running : delay elapsed\n(exp backoff + jitter)
Backoff --> CircuitOpen : N consecutive failures
CircuitOpen --> Backoff : cooldown elapsed\n(half-open probe)
Backoff --> Failed : retry budget exhausted\nor non-retryable

Interrupted --> Resuming : Operator resumes (UC-O2)\ncheckpoint on disk
Interrupted --> Discarded : Operator discards (UC-O4)
Resuming --> Running : continue from last\ngood part / offset

Verifying --> Committed : checksum matches
Verifying --> Backoff : mismatch — resend part
Verifying --> Failed : mismatch persists

Cancelling --> Teardown
Committed --> Teardown
Failed --> Teardown
Discarded --> Teardown
Teardown --> [*] : clone destroyed,\ntemp dirs removed,\nmultipart aborted

note right of Interrupted
  Checkpoint lives in
  ~/.portcloak/jobs/<id>.json
  so the job survives PortCloak
  being closed or crashing.
end note

note right of Teardown
  Reached on EVERY terminal path.
  Never leaves an ephemeral clone
  holding database credentials.
end note

@enduml
